## Setting Up Tomcat Server
1. Download tomcat zip file
2. Create tomcat-users.xml file in conf directory
    <user username="admin" passwords="admin1234" roles="admin-gui, manager-gui"/>
3. Create a shortcut for starting tomcat
    sudo ln -s /opt/apche/bin/startup.sh /usr/bin/startTomcat
    sudo ln -s /opt/apche/bin/shutdow.sh /usr/bin/stopTomcat
4. sudo vi /opt/apache/webapps/manager/META_INF/context.xml
    comment:
    <!-- Value className="org.apache.catalina.values.RemoteAddrValue">
    allow="127\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|::| 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1"/>-->
4. sudo vi /opt/apache/webapps/host-manager/META_INF/context.xml
    comment:
    <!-- Value className="org.apache.catalina.values.RemoteAddrValue">
    allow="127\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|::| 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1"/>-->




##  Generate war file from springboot
1. Open pom.xml add this below <version></version>
    <packaging>war</packaging>
2. Dependency Config
<dependencies>
    <!-- Web dependency without embedded Tomcat -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        <exclusions>
            <exclusion>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-tomcat</artifactId>
            </exclusion>
        </exclusions>
    </dependency>

    <!-- Provided scope for servlet container (Tomcat, etc.) -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-tomcat</artifactId>
        <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
</dependencies>

3. Update Main Class  
<!-- Extend SpringBootServletInitializer and override configure(): -->
import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.builder.SpringApplicationBuilder;
import org.springframework.boot.web.servlet.support.SpringBootServletInitializer;

@SpringBootApplication
public class YourApplication extends SpringBootServletInitializer {

    @Override
    protected SpringApplicationBuilder configure(SpringApplicationBuilder builder) {
        return builder.sources(YourApplication.class);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(YourApplication.class, args);
    }
}

4. Build the WAR
mvn clean package

5. .WAR file in target folder
If you still see a .jar, double-check:

You saved the pom.xml with <packaging>war</packaging>

You ran mvn clean package (not just mvn package)

Your project is not being overridden by some parent POM defaults (you can check in target/classes/META-INF for any hints)




copy the .war file and store in tomcat/webapps folder